    "notes": "Real shaadi season kitty: the morning after a sangeet everyone turns up with wet mehendi, and the meme (somebody else must do everything) is known to every viewer. Myra is the playbook's 'stuck with the job' girl, so the game is in character. Chip counts her chores every shot so a muted viewer sees the stake climb. Escalation ordinary, ordinary, absurd (nose with a dabber). Claim before reveal on the twist: 'Full House! Full House!' then 'Ticket kiska hai?' / 'Ruhi ka.' The flip is a see-it prize envelope that goes into Myra's bag. Button repeats the opening line word for word with the opposite meaning, so the reel loops. Three endings tried: Ruhi simply wins (flat, Myra just loses), Myra gets her own mehendi done next kitty (needs a time jump), Myra keeps the prize till it dries (kept: kind revenge, loops). Rewrote once: first draft had Shruti as the helper and Myra with mehendi, but the playbook gives the stuck-with-the-job role to Myra. Shots stay at 2 lines and 8 words or fewer, no silenceBefore, no ellipses."
